Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.12), python3-yaml, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gnome-shell (>= 50), gnome-shell (<< 51), maluos-desktop-branding (>= 0.3.2)
Recommends: maluos-gateway (>= 0.3.2), maluos-vault (>= 0.3.0), maluos-agent (>= 0.2.1), maluos-firstboot (>= 0.1.7), maluos-desk (>= 0.1.0), gnome-software, xdg-terminal-exec
Description: MaluOS agent-aware session: indicator, notifications, session service
 A per-user service (com.maluos.Session on the session bus, D-Bus
 activated) that reads what the OS already knows about this desk: the
 agents on the host and their units, the inference gateway with its
 backends, queue and the user's own policy and spend, the user's vault
 secrets and delegations, their alerts in the ledger, and the memory host
 this desk runs. It talks to the gateway and the vault over their sockets
 as the session user, so peer identity applies and no token lives in the
 session. State changes become desktop notifications.
 .
 The GNOME Shell extension maluos-session@maluos.com puts that state in
 the top panel: an indicator with a menu of agents (start, stop, restart,
 logs through polkit), gateway and budget, vault, recent calls and alerts.
 .
 Agents carry their owner; the owner's session controls them without an
 administrator's password. A vault grant request (an agent refused one of
 your secrets) becomes a notification with Allow and Deny. The MaluOS Desk
 window (maluos-desk, GTK 4 and libadwaita) shows the same state in full.
 .
 Software updates: the state carries what `maluctl update status` reports
 (pending updates by source, the automatic policy, a due restart); updates
 that wait for the user become one notification whose Install button opens
 GNOME Software's updates page, and the Desk's System page shows them.
 .
 The office: on a desk enrolled with a Business OS office (maluos-desk,
 maluctl office) the service heartbeats the office while the person is
 signed in and says offline when the session ends, so the office's estate
 shows the desk's presence; the indicator and the Desk show the office,
 what it publishes to desks, and whether it still accepts this desk.
